---@field name? aws.imagebuilder.WorkflowStepName The name of the specified runtime instance of the workflow step.
---@field description? aws.imagebuilder.WorkflowStepDescription Describes the specified workflow step.
---@field action? aws.imagebuilder.WorkflowStepAction The name of the action that the specified step performs.
---@field status? aws.imagebuilder.WorkflowStepExecutionStatus The current status for the specified runtime instance of the workflow step.
---@field rollbackStatus? aws.imagebuilder.WorkflowStepExecutionRollbackStatus Reports on the rollback status of the specified runtime instance of the workflow step, if applicable. Rollback runs when the workflow execution fails, and undoes the work that completed steps performed.
---@field message? aws.imagebuilder.WorkflowStepMessage The output message from the specified runtime instance of the workflow step, if applicable.
---@field inputs? aws.imagebuilder.WorkflowStepInputs Input parameters that Image Builder provided for the specified runtime instance of the workflow step, as a JSON-encoded string.
---@field outputs? aws.imagebuilder.WorkflowStepOutputs The output values that the specified runtime instance of the workflow step produced, as a JSON-encoded string. For example, a step that launches an instance outputs the instance ID. If the step failed, this field contains the error message.
---@field startTime? aws.imagebuilder.DateTime The timestamp when the specified runtime instance of the workflow step started.
---@field endTime? aws.imagebuilder.DateTime The timestamp when the specified runtime instance of the workflow step finished.
---@field onFailure? aws.imagebuilder.NonEmptyString The action that the workflow takes if this step fails, as configured in the workflow document. Abort fails the workflow and rolls back completed steps. Continue proceeds to the next step. If the step doesn't set a value, it defaults to Abort.
---@field timeoutSeconds? aws.imagebuilder.WorkflowStepTimeoutSecondsInteger The maximum duration in seconds for this step to complete its action. If the workflow document doesn't set a timeout for the step, Image Builder applies the default timeout for the step's action. This field returns that value.
---@field attemptNumber? aws.imagebuilder.WorkflowStepAttemptCount The current attempt number for the specified runtime instance of the workflow step. The first run is attempt one. The number increases by one for each retry.
---@field maxAttempts? aws.imagebuilder.WorkflowStepAttemptCount The maximum number of attempts allowed for the specified runtime instance of the workflow step, based on the retry configuration in the workflow document. If the step doesn't configure retries, the maximum is one attempt.

