---@field sourcePipelineName? aws.imagebuilder.ResourceName The name of the image pipeline that created this image. Image Builder doesn't return this field for new images. Use sourcePipelineArn instead.
---@field sourcePipelineArn? aws.imagebuilder.Arn The Amazon Resource Name (ARN) of the image pipeline that created this image. This field is only present for images that a pipeline execution created.
---@field infrastructureConfiguration? aws.imagebuilder.InfrastructureConfiguration The infrastructure that Image Builder used to create this image.
---@field distributionConfiguration? aws.imagebuilder.DistributionConfiguration The distribution configuration that Image Builder used to create this image.
---@field imageTestsConfiguration? aws.imagebuilder.ImageTestsConfiguration The image test settings that Image Builder used when it created this image.
---@field dateCreated? aws.imagebuilder.DateTime The date on which Image Builder created this image.
---@field outputResources? aws.imagebuilder.OutputResources The output resources that Image Builder produces for this image.
---@field tags? aws.imagebuilder.TagMap The tags that apply to this image.
---@field buildType? aws.imagebuilder.BuildType Indicates the type of build that created this image. The build can be initiated in the following ways:
---@field imageSource? aws.imagebuilder.ImageSource The origin of the base image that Image Builder used to build this image.
---@field scanState? aws.imagebuilder.ImageScanState Contains information about the current state of scans for this image.
---@field imageScanningConfiguration? aws.imagebuilder.ImageScanningConfiguration The settings that determine whether and how Amazon Inspector scans this image.
---@field deprecationTime? aws.imagebuilder.DateTimeTimestamp The time when deprecation occurs for an image resource. This can be a past or future date.
---@field lifecycleExecutionId? aws.imagebuilder.LifecycleExecutionId Identifies the last runtime instance of the lifecycle policy to take action on the image.
---@field executionRole? aws.imagebuilder.RoleNameOrArn The name or Amazon Resource Name (ARN) for the IAM role you create that grants Image Builder access to perform workflow actions.
---@field workflows? aws.imagebuilder.WorkflowConfigurationList The build, test, and distribution workflow configurations that are associated with the image.
---@field loggingConfiguration? aws.imagebuilder.ImageLoggingConfiguration The logging configuration that's defined for the image. Image Builder uses the defined settings to direct execution log output during image creation.

