---@field uri? aws.imagebuilder.Uri The uri of the component. Must be an Amazon S3 URL and you must have permission to access the Amazon S3 bucket. If you use Amazon S3, you can specify component content up to your service quota. Either data or uri can be used to specify the data within the component.
---@field kmsKeyId? aws.imagebuilder.NonEmptyString The Amazon Resource Name (ARN) of the KMS key that is used to encrypt this component. This can be either the Key ARN or the Alias ARN. For more information, see Key identifiers (KeyId) in the Key Management Service Developer Guide. If you don't specify a key, Image Builder encrypts the component data with a KMS key that Image Builder owns.
